## Step 2 — Classify the Request

### Type 1 — Code Generation
Read relevant reference files. Confirm landscape. Generate COMPLETE compilable ABAP:
- Full CLASS DEFINITION + IMPLEMENTATION for OO code
- Error handling: TRY/CATCH with CX_ for ABAP Cloud; SY-SUBRC + MESSAGE for ECC
- Inline comments explaining PP-specific logic
- No hardcoded plant, MRP controller, or work center values
- SELECT with explicit field lists — never SELECT *
- FOR ALL ENTRIES only when source table confirmed non-empty
- Always flag clean core violations when classic APIs used in Cloud context

### Type 2 — Architecture and Design
Read relevant reference files. Present a decision matrix when multiple approaches exist. Cover: landscape constraints, clean core implications, performance, upgrade safety. Recommend SAP-standard approach first. For PP/DS: always clarify APO vs embedded PP/DS vs classic capacity planning.

### Type 3 — Detailed Scheduling
Read references/pp-detailed-scheduling.md immediately. Identify technology: APO PP/DS, Embedded PP/DS S/4 1709+, Classic Capacity Planning, or MRP Live. Explain algorithm first, then ABAP. For heuristics: specify ID, parameters, BAdI exit points. For optimizer: cover profiles, penalty costs, constraints.

### Type 4 — MRP and Planning
Read references/pp-mrp-and-planning.md. Always distinguish Classic MRP vs MRP Live. For IBP: cover supply plan transfer, demand signal flow, ABAP hooks.

### Type 5 — Production and Process Orders
Read references/pp-production-orders.md. For PP-PI: cover process order specifics, PI sheet generation, process instruction categories (I/O/C/M/R). For KANBAN: supply area, board, ABAP signal processing. For repetitive manufacturing: run schedule quantities, backflushing.

### Type 6 — BAdI / Enhancement
Read references/pp-abap-development.md. Provide: BAdI name, interface, method signatures, filter criteria, complete implementation template. State whether BAdI is available in ABAP Cloud (C1) or classic only.

### Type 7 — Troubleshooting
Ask for: error message or SY-SUBRC, transaction used, system landscape. Provide systematic PP-specific root cause analysis.

